# <type>(<scope>): <short summary in imperative mood, max 50 chars>
#
# Pick a commit type:
#   feat:     New feature, endpoint, worker, or capability
#   fix:      Bug fix, race condition patch, or connection leak fix
#   refactor: Code restructuring without changing behavior
#   perf:     Query optimization, caching, or throughput improvement
#   test:     Adding or updating pytest / testcontainers suites
#   docs:     README, Mermaid diagrams, or API doc updates
#   ci:       GitHub Actions workflows, ruff, or pre-commit config
#   chore:    Dependencies (uv.lock), Dockerfiles, or .env.example
#
# Common scopes: api, worker, db, redis, di, config, docker, tests
#
# Examples:
#   feat(worker): add SKIP LOCKED outbox polling loop
#   fix(di): close asyncpg/psycopg pool cleanly on lifespan exit
#   test(api): verify redis sliding-window rate limit with testcontainers
#
# Optional body (explain WHY, not just what):
#